# Lifecycle fixture: raised cell

Checked-in input for `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_runner_test.exs`, not a
cookbook. Its first cell leaves an unlinked process and its second cell
raises, so the runner must report the failed cell and still reclaim the
process.

```elixir
unlinked = spawn(fn -> receive do: (:release -> :ok) end)
send(observer, {:raise_fixture, unlinked})
```

```elixir
raise ArgumentError, "lifecycle fixture failure"
```
